# UI — Apple-inspired

Visual north star: **Apple** (quiet hierarchy, soft selection, no shouty chrome).
Also borrow restraint from Claude/Google: clarity over decoration.

User preference (locked): prefer Apple HIG over “more contrast / louder chrome”
fixes. When readability and quiet select conflict, keep quiet select and nudge
type color one step only (`--faint` ↔ `--muted`) — never add ink borders,
inset bars, or accent colors for secondary UI.

## Tokens (already in `global.scss`)

Prefer `--bg --ink --muted --faint --line --soft --fill`. Do not invent new
purples/creams, accent blues for chrome, or multi-layer glows.

## Selection / chips / tabs

Quiet select — never inverted black pills for secondary controls.

```scss
/* ✅ selected */
background: var(--fill);
color: var(--ink);
font-weight: 400; /* or 500 max */

/* ❌ avoid */
background: var(--ink);
color: #fff;
font-weight: 600+;
box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px …; /* double-ring “loud” select */
border: 1px solid var(--ink); /* ring select on chips */
/* left ink bar / ::before accent on list rows */
```

- Default chips: often **borderless**, muted text; hover → `--soft`
- Active: `--fill` + ink text; **no bold bump** just to mark selected
- Primary CTA (发送 / 确认) may stay solid `--ink` — that’s intentional Apple

## Type

- Body / chips: `400`; section labels: `500` or small caps + `--faint`
- Titles (modal/page): `600` OK; don’t bold every interactive label
- Prefer `letter-spacing: -0.01em` on UI labels; anti-aliased system stack

## Motion & chrome

- Transitions ~`0.15s–0.2s ease`; no bounce / glow / emoji decoration
- Hover: soft fill or ink color shift — **not** danger-red wash on delete
- Avoid card stacks + lift (`translateY` + heavy shadow) for simple lists;
  prefer hairline `--line` or `--soft` fill
- Destructive confirm: use shared `Modal` + `btn-ink`, not `window.confirm`

## When unsure

Match `ChatPage` mention chips / workflow tabs after the Apple pass — those are
the reference selected states.
